    "norm": "Verifies that {@code CharRange.isNotIn('a', 'a')} produces a negated single-character range — i.e. a range that excludes only 'a' and includes every other character. <p>When both endpoints are identical the range is collapsed to a single character, so {@code start} and {@code end} must both equal 'a'. Because the range is negated the string representation uses the '^' prefix.</p>"
